.Dd August 20, 2026
.Dt WP 1
.Os WordProcess 1.0
.
.Sh NAME
.Nm wp
.Nd keyboard-focused console word processor
.
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl 8hrv
.Op Fl -no-unicode
.Op Fl -no-ncurses-colour
.Op Fl -config Ar file.lua
.Op Ar file.wp
.Nm
.Fl c | Fl -convert
.Ar source destination
.Nm
.Fl -lua Ar file.lua
.Op Ar argument ...
.Nm
.Fl -exec Ar command
.Op Ar argument ...
.
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the ncurses frontend for WordProcess, a Unicode-aware word processor for
structured and long-form writing.
A native
.Pa .wp
file is a document set containing one or more named documents, styles,
settings, page layouts, and add-on state.
.
.Pp
With no file,
.Nm
loads the default template or creates a blank set.
If the named file does not exist, its path is retained as the destination for
the first save.
Press Escape to open the menu.
.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print command-line help and exit.
.It Fl v , Fl -version
Print the application version and exit.
.It Fl c , Fl -convert Ar source destination
Convert between formats selected from their filename extensions and exit.
.It Fl -lua Ar file.lua
Load and execute a Lua file, passing all remaining arguments to it, then exit.
.It Fl -exec Ar command
Execute a Lua source string, passing all remaining arguments to it, then exit.
.It Fl -config Ar file.lua
Use this startup configuration file instead of the default.
.It Fl r , Fl -recent
Open the most recently used native file.
.It Fl 8 , Fl -no-unicode
Use an ISO-8859-1-compatible display character set instead of Unicode glyphs.
.It Fl -no-ncurses-colour
Accepted for compatibility; currently has no effect.
.El
.
.Sh CONVERSION
Input extensions are
.Pa wp , txt , md , html ,
and
.Pa odt .
Output additionally supports
.Pa org , tex ,
and
.Pa tr .
Extensions are case-sensitive.
.
.Pp
Append
.Sq : Ns Ar name
to native input to select a document from a set:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
wp --convert 'book.wp:Chapter 1' chapter1.odt
.Ed
For non-native input the suffix assigns a name to the imported document.
The output must not have a document-name suffix.
.
.Sh KEY BINDINGS
.Ss Compact keyboards
Hold Ctrl-Alt and press a command key. These direct chords do not replace any
conventional Ctrl shortcut or Alt menu accelerator.
.Bl -tag -width Shift-X
.It H , J , K , L
Move left, down, up, or right.
.It B , W
Move to the previous or next word.
.It I , O
Move to the previous or next inserted tabulation.
.It A , E
Move to the beginning or end of the display line.
.It U , D
Move one screen page up or down.
.It T , G
Move to the beginning or end of the document.
.It X , Shift-X
Delete the next or previous character.
.It Shift-D
Delete the current paragraph.
.It ?
Open the in-program keyboard reference.
.El
.Ss Conventional bindings
.Bl -tag -width Ctrl-Right
.It Escape
Open the menu.
.It H , J , K , L (in menus)
Navigate left, down, up, or right, alongside the arrow keys.
.It ? (in the main menu)
Open the in-program keyboard reference.
.It Ctrl-S , Ctrl-O , Ctrl-Q
Save, open, and exit.
.It Arrow keys
Move by display line or character.
.It Ctrl-Left , Ctrl-Right
Move by word.
.It Ctrl-Up , Ctrl-Down
Move by paragraph.
.It Home , End
Move to a display-line boundary.
.It Ctrl-Home , Ctrl-End
Move to a document boundary.
.It Shift plus movement
Extend the selection.
.It Ctrl-X , Ctrl-C , Ctrl-V
Cut, copy, and paste.
.It Ctrl-Z , Ctrl-Y
Undo and redo.
.It Ctrl-F , Ctrl-K , Ctrl-R
Find, find next, and replace then find.
.It Ctrl-B , Ctrl-I , Ctrl-U , Ctrl-N
Apply bold, italic, underline, or normal character style.
.It Ctrl-P
Choose a paragraph style.
.El
.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width ~/.wordprocess/user.dictionary
.It Pa ~/.wordprocess/startup.lua
Default trusted Lua startup file.
.It Pa ~/.wordprocess/settings.dat
Serialised global settings.
.It Pa ~/.wordprocess/templates/
Template directory.
.It Pa ~/.wordprocess/templates/default.wp
Optional template for new sets.
.It Pa ~/.wordprocess/user.dictionary
User spelling dictionary.
.El
.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width USERPROFILE
.It Ev HOME
Used to locate the configuration directory on Unix.
.It Ev USERPROFILE
Fallback home directory on systems without
.Ev HOME .
.El
.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
Conversion and script failures exit nonzero and print a diagnostic prefixed
with
.Dq wp: .
.
